.TH WS2SOCKET 1 "September 2026" "ws2socket 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ws2socket \- WebSocket to TCP socket proxy with static file serving
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ws2socket
.RB [ \-l
.IR host [: port ]]
.RB [ \-p
.IR port ]
.RB { \-t
.IR host : port
|
.B \-\-token\-file
.IR file }
.RB [ \-w
.IR dir ]
.RB [ \-f
.IR file ]
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ws2socket
accepts WebSocket (RFC 6455) connections and forwards the traffic,
bidirectionally and unmodified, to a TCP server.
It can also serve static files over HTTP, which makes it a drop\-in
companion for the noVNC browser VNC client.
.PP
It is a C implementation of the ideas behind the Python
.B websockify
project, intended for embedded Linux systems (for example Yocto\-based
images) where a Python runtime is not available.
It depends only on the C library, POSIX threads, OpenSSL and zlib.
.PP
Each accepted client is handled in a separate child process.
Plain HTTP requests are answered from the web root (or with
.B 426 Upgrade Required
when no web root is set).
WebSocket upgrade requests on any path are accepted and bridged to the
configured target, or to the target named by the client's token when a
token file is used.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print version, copyright and license information and exit.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-listen " \fIhost\fR[:\fIport\fR] | \fIport\fR"
Address to listen on.
A bare number is taken as the port; IPv6 addresses are written in
brackets, for example \fB[::1]:6080\fR.
Default: \fB0.0.0.0:6080\fR.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-port " \fIport\fR"
Port to listen on (alternative to giving it in \fB\-\-listen\fR).
Default: \fB6080\fR.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-target " \fIhost\fR:\fIport\fR"
TCP server that WebSocket traffic is forwarded to, for example a VNC
server at \fB127.0.0.1:5900\fR.
Either a target or a token file is required.
.TP
.BI \-\-token\-file " file"
Choose the target for each client from \fIfile\fR instead of using a
single \fB\-\-target\fR.
See
.B TOKEN FILE
below.
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-web\-root " \fIdir\fR"
Serve static files from \fIdir\fR for non\-WebSocket HTTP requests.
A request for a path ending in \fB/\fR is served \fBindex.html\fR.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-config " \fIfile\fR"
Read settings from an INI\-style configuration file.
See
.B CONFIGURATION FILE
below.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-cert " \fIfile\fR"
TLS certificate in PEM format.
With \fB\-\-cert\fR and \fB\-\-key\fR, all connections use TLS
(\fBhttps://\fR and \fBwss://\fR); plain connections are refused.
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-key " \fIfile\fR"
TLS private key in PEM format.
Required together with \fB\-\-cert\fR.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Set the log level to \fBdebug\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-log\-file " file"
Also append log messages to \fIfile\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-daemon
Detach from the terminal and run in the background.
.TP
.BI \-\-pid\-file " file"
When running with \fB\-\-daemon\fR, write the daemon's process ID to
\fIfile\fR.
.SH CONFIGURATION FILE
The file given with \fB\-\-config\fR uses \fIkey\fR = \fIvalue\fR lines
grouped in sections.
Text after \fB#\fR or \fB;\fR is a comment.
Boolean values accept \fBtrue\fR/\fBfalse\fR, \fByes\fR/\fBno\fR,
\fBon\fR/\fBoff\fR or \fB1\fR/\fB0\fR.
An invalid value is an error.
.PP
Command\-line options take precedence over values in the file.
.TP
.B [general]
.nf
daemon     = false
pid_file   = /var/run/ws2socket.pid
token_file = /etc/ws2socket/tokens
.fi
.TP
.B [server]
.nf
listen          = 0.0.0.0:6080
port            = 6080
cert_file       = /etc/ssl/certs/ws2socket.crt
key_file        = /etc/ssl/private/ws2socket.key
max_connections = 1024
socket_timeout  = 60
web_root        = /usr/share/novnc
.fi
.TP
.B [proxy]
.nf
target          = 127.0.0.1:5900
buffer_size     = 1048576
socket_timeout  = 60
.fi
.TP
.B [logging]
.nf
level   = info        ; debug, info, warning, error, critical
file    = /var/log/ws2socket.log
console = true
syslog  = false
.fi
.PP
The numeric values shown are the built\-in defaults:
.TP
.B [server] max_connections
Maximum number of simultaneous clients (0 for no limit).
Further clients are answered with \fB503 Service Unavailable\fR.
.TP
.B [server] socket_timeout
Seconds a client may take to complete the TLS handshake, send its HTTP
request, or finish sending a frame, and to accept data.
0 disables the timeout.
.TP
.B [proxy] buffer_size
Largest WebSocket message, in bytes, accepted from a client (after
decompression).
Larger messages close the connection with status 1009.
.TP
.B [proxy] socket_timeout
Seconds allowed for connecting to the target and for the target to
accept data.
.PP
An annotated example is shipped as \fBws2socket.conf.example\fR.
.SH TOKEN FILE
With \fB\-\-token\-file\fR (or \fBtoken_file\fR in \fB[general]\fR),
each client selects its target with a token, using the same format as
websockify's \fBTokenFile\fR plugin:
.PP
.RS
.nf
# token: host:port
desktop1: 192.168.1.10:5900
desktop2: 192.168.1.11:5900
.fi
.RE
.PP
The token is taken from the \fBtoken\fR query parameter
(\fB/websockify?token=desktop1\fR) or, failing that, from the first path
component (\fB/desktop1\fR).
Requests with a missing or unknown token are answered with
\fB403 Forbidden\fR.
If \fIfile\fR is a directory, every file in it is read.
Changes are picked up automatically within about a minute.
.PP
In noVNC, pass the token through the \fBpath\fR parameter, for example
\fBvnc.html?path=websockify%3Ftoken%3Ddesktop1\fR.
.SH PROTOCOL SUPPORT
.IP \(bu 2
RFC 6455 handshake, framing (7\-, 16\- and 64\-bit lengths) and
client\-to\-server unmasking.
.IP \(bu 2
Text, binary and fragmented (continuation) messages.
.IP \(bu 2
Ping frames are answered with pong; close frames are echoed and end the
session.
.IP \(bu 2
permessage\-deflate compression (RFC 7692), negotiated only when the
client offers it.
Data sent to the client is not compressed.
.IP \(bu 2
HTTP/1.1 static file serving with MIME types for HTML, CSS, JavaScript,
JSON, PNG, JPEG, GIF, SVG, ICO, WASM and plain text; other files are
sent as \fBapplication/octet\-stream\fR.
Paths containing \fB..\fR are rejected.
.IP \(bu 2
Error responses: \fB403\fR (bad token or path), \fB404\fR,
\fB426\fR (no web root), \fB502\fR (target unreachable),
\fB503\fR (connection limit reached).
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.BR SIGINT ", " SIGTERM
Stop accepting connections and exit.
.TP
.B SIGPIPE
Ignored.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Normal termination.
.TP
.B 1
Invalid arguments or configuration, or a startup failure.
.SH EXAMPLES
Proxy WebSocket clients to a local VNC server and serve noVNC:
.PP
.RS
.nf
ws2socket \-\-listen 0.0.0.0:6080 \-\-target 127.0.0.1:5900 \e
          \-\-web\-root /usr/share/novnc
.fi
.RE
.PP
Then open \fBhttp://\fIhost\fB:6080/vnc.html\fR in a browser.
.PP
Run in the background from a configuration file:
.PP
.RS
.nf
ws2socket \-\-config /etc/ws2socket.conf \-\-daemon \e
          \-\-pid\-file /var/run/ws2socket.pid
.fi
.RE
.PP
Serve \fBwss://\fR and \fBhttps://\fR with a certificate:
.PP
.RS
.nf
ws2socket \-\-cert /etc/ssl/certs/vnc.pem \-\-key /etc/ssl/private/vnc.key \e
          \-\-target 127.0.0.1:5900 \-\-web\-root /usr/share/novnc
.fi
.RE
.PP
Route clients to several VNC servers by token:
.PP
.RS
.nf
ws2socket \-\-token\-file /etc/ws2socket/tokens \-\-web\-root /usr/share/novnc
.fi
.RE
.PP
Debug a connection:
.PP
.RS
.nf
ws2socket \-t 127.0.0.1:5900 \-v \-\-log\-file /tmp/ws2socket.log
.fi
.RE
.SH SECURITY
.B ws2socket
does not authenticate users.
Without a token file, anyone who can reach the listening port can open a
connection to the target; with one, anyone who knows a token can.
Treat tokens as secrets, use TLS so they are not sent in the clear, and
restrict access with a firewall or a reverse proxy such as
.BR nginx (8)
that adds authentication.
Keep the target service's own authentication (for example a VNC
password) enabled.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/ws2socket.conf
Conventional location of the configuration file.
It is only read when named with \fB\-\-config\fR.
.TP
.I ws2socket.conf.example
Annotated example configuration, in the source distribution.
.SH BUGS
.IP \(bu 2
The HTTP server is minimal: no keep\-alive, \fBHEAD\fR or range
requests, and URL\-encoded file names are not decoded.
.IP \(bu 2
Metrics are collected internally but not exported.
.PP
